{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-memory-chips-shortage-dram-nand-hbm-and-what-is-happening-now/audio/main-ea6fae3e572b.mp3","durationSec":316.632,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.04,"text":"Memory chips hold information inside electronic devices."},{"start":3.6,"end":7.16,"text":"Three important types are DRAM, NAND, and HBM."},{"start":7.76,"end":8.66,"text":"They do different jobs."},{"start":9.56,"end":12.36,"text":"DRAM is short-term working memory, often called RAM."},{"start":12.96,"end":15.18,"text":"It holds information that a device is using now."},{"start":15.96,"end":19.66,"text":"Think of it as a kitchen work surface, with everything ready for the current job."},{"start":20.58,"end":21.96,"text":"NAND is long-term storage."},{"start":22.42,"end":25.66,"text":"It keeps photos, apps, and files even when the power is off."},{"start":26.2,"end":29.78,"text":"Phones and solid-state drives, or SSDs, use NAND."},{"start":30.52,"end":32.7,"text":"HBM means high-bandwidth memory."},{"start":33.3,"end":37.5,"text":"It stacks DRAM chips on top of each other and moves information very quickly."},{"start":38.52,"end":42.62,"text":"AI systems use it to keep their powerful processing chips supplied with information."},{"start":43.48,"end":47.92,"text":"An AI data center is a building full of server computers that run AI services."},{"start":48.74,"end":55,"text":"These computers need memory for larger AI models, longer conversations, and many users at the same time."},{"start":55,"end":59.16,"text":"AI agents, which carry out tasks, add more demand."},{"start":59.96,"end":63.26,"text":"Fast processing chips also need information to arrive quickly."},{"start":64.06,"end":65.7,"text":"HBM helps meet that need."},{"start":66.48,"end":71.1,"text":"As AI server demand grows, factories put more effort into making HBM."},{"start":72.54,"end":76.3,"text":"A wafer is a thin, round piece of material on which chips are made."},{"start":77.22,"end":80.14,"text":"HBM needs more wafer space than ordinary DRAM."},{"start":80.99,"end":86.28,"text":"Samsung says HBM uses about 20% of global DRAM wafer capacity now."},{"start":87.16,"end":92.8,"text":"That share could reach close to 30% in 2027, leaving less capacity for other memory."},{"start":93.4,"end":95.92,"text":"The pressure was already clear in late 2025."},{"start":97.1,"end":101.46,"text":"PC and phone makers shipped devices early to avoid later memory price rises."},{"start":102.64,"end":106,"text":"In 2026, memory became more expensive."},{"start":106.92,"end":110.86,"text":"A contract price is a price agreed between a supplier and a buyer."},{"start":111.3,"end":121.32,"text":"The contract price of a 16-gigabit DDR5 DRAM chip reached $48 in September 2026, up from $45 in July."},{"start":122.38,"end":125.54,"text":"Further increases are forecasts, not completed changes."},{"start":126.56,"end":136.44,"text":"TrendForce expects ordinary DRAM contract prices to rise another 10–15% in late 2026, and NAND prices by 15–20%."},{"start":136.68,"end":143.08,"text":"For 2027, it forecasts a 121% rise in HBM’s average selling price."},{"start":143.8,"end":155.04,"text":"Separately, industry estimates suggest a 12-high, 36GB HBM4 stack could rise from about $600 in 2026 to about $1,300 in 2027."},{"start":155.86,"end":163.44,"text":"Three companies effectively share the HBM market: SK hynix, Samsung Electronics, and Micron Technology."},{"start":164.36,"end":166.28,"text":"SK hynix remains the leader."},{"start":166.74,"end":170.84,"text":"In the second quarter of 2026, it had about 50% of HBM revenue."},{"start":171.76,"end":173.02,"text":"Samsung is catching up fast."},{"start":173.64,"end":178.88,"text":"Its share rose from 21% to 33% in the comparison reported by Counterpoint Research."},{"start":179.92,"end":185.48,"text":"Both Samsung and SK hynix began mass-production shipments of HBM4 in 2026."},{"start":186.54,"end":190.7,"text":"Micron already has contracts for most of its 2027 HBM output."},{"start":191.1,"end":194.54,"text":"That means much of next year’s supply already has buyers."},{"start":194.54,"end":196.92,"text":"The shortage also reaches NAND."},{"start":197.68,"end":205.14,"text":"Japan’s Kioxia said in January that its whole 2026 NAND flash production was already sold out."},{"start":205.14,"end":209.28,"text":"AI demand affects storage as well as working memory."},{"start":209.92,"end":213.66,"text":"More factories sound like a simple answer, but building them takes years."},{"start":214.62,"end":219.38,"text":"Memory production needs special buildings, equipment, and carefully controlled conditions."},{"start":219.38,"end":223.16,"text":"Even after a factory is ready, production grows slowly."},{"start":223.94,"end":229.04,"text":"Micron CEO Sanjay Mehrotra says the balance between supply and demand is getting tighter."},{"start":229.86,"end":234.4,"text":"Micron and Samsung executives expect the shortage to continue into 2028."},{"start":235.2,"end":241.5,"text":"Micron plans new clean rooms in 2028, but those rooms will not immediately produce memory at full speed."},{"start":242.9,"end":245.44,"text":"Meanwhile, the business is growing sharply."},{"start":246.22,"end":255.04,"text":"South Korea’s memory chip exports rose 358.6% in September 2026 compared with a year earlier."},{"start":256.02,"end":258.74,"text":"Strong export growth can happen alongside a shortage."},{"start":259.72,"end":265.34,"text":"Suppliers can earn more while buyers struggle with higher prices and limited supply."},{"start":265.9,"end":270.2,"text":"The shortage reaches ordinary shops through higher prices and smaller memory amounts."},{"start":271.02,"end":274.72,"text":"PCs and phones may cost more, or offer less at the same price."},{"start":275.72,"end":277.08,"text":"IDC gives a clear example."},{"start":277.08,"end":287.84,"text":"A phone that previously offered 12GB of RAM and 256GB of storage may offer only 8GB and 128GB at the same price."},{"start":288.62,"end":292.16,"text":"PCs may also come with less RAM and smaller SSDs."},{"start":292.8,"end":294.48,"text":"Cheaper devices are especially affected."},{"start":295.46,"end":297.38,"text":"There are fewer consumer choices, too."},{"start":298.42,"end":303.54,"text":"Micron announced in December 2025 that its Crucial brand would stop selling RAM to consumers."},{"start":304.52,"end":306.72,"text":"These changes make replacement less attractive."},{"start":307.58,"end":311.16,"text":"Many people may keep old devices longer or buy used phones."},{"start":311.88,"end":315.96,"text":"The important comparison is now both price and what that price includes."}],"words":[{"text":"Memory","start":0,"end":0.3},{"text":"chips","start":0.3,"end":0.56},{"text":"hold","start":0.56,"end":0.9},{"text":"information","start":0.9,"end":1.4},{"text":"inside","start":1.4,"end":1.98},{"text":"electronic","start":1.98,"end":2.46},{"text":"devices","start":2.46,"end":3.04},{"text":"Three","start":3.6,"end":3.86},{"text":"important","start":3.86,"end":4.22},{"text":"types","start":4.22,"end":4.64},{"text":"are","start":4.64,"end":5.08},{"text":"DRAM","start":5.08,"end":5.42},{"text":"NAND","start":6.02,"end":6.16},{"text":"and","start":6.46,"end":6.6},{"text":"HBM","start":6.6,"end":7.16},{"text":"They","start":7.76,"end":7.92},{"text":"do","start":7.92,"end":8.08},{"text":"different","start":8.08,"end":8.34},{"text":"jobs","start":8.34,"end":8.66},{"text":"DRAM","start":9.56,"end":9.64},{"text":"is","start":9.64,"end":9.92},{"text":"short-term","start":9.92,"end":10.4},{"text":"working","start":10.4,"end":10.72},{"text":"memory","start":10.72,"end":11.14},{"text":"often","start":11.54,"end":11.74},{"text":"called","start":11.74,"end":12.06},{"text":"RAM","start":12.06,"end":12.36},{"text":"It","start":12.96,"end":13.08},{"text":"holds","start":13.08,"end":13.34},{"text":"information","start":13.34,"end":13.78},{"text":"that","start":13.